              "author": "doctorzook",
              "body": "Microsoft offers mass buyouts for roughly a quarter of its workforce\nEx-MSFT here. I resigned in June, I was an L63. I spent 8 years at MSFT across two stints.\nMy last 18 months at MSFT were deeply unproductive. Constant reorgs, the work not being aligned to my capabilities and unfortunately just the general feeling that I was under worked and had very little opportu... 60k workers, 1/4 of the workers. This is a big deal. It also really puts you into a bind if you receive the offer. Do you accept, take the money, and hope you can find a job  (Now competing with many other Msft employees that are looking). Do you decline and hope you don't get hit with the layoff wh... The mass buyout offer to 25% of Microsoft's workforce comes less than a week after Microsoft President Brad Smith proclaimed to employees: 'We stand by our people. We always have. We always will.' in a video he posted to LinkedIn.\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7518428...",
